 is the strongest option. It wins the Queen for free, strengthens Black's center by placing a pawn on d6 (supporting e5), and defends the Bishop at c5. It also keeps the Black King safer and the Black Queen reserved for later action.\nReason: Taking the unsupported Queen leads to a winning material advantage. Capturing with the pawn (`P: c7-d6`) is strategically best as it improves pawn structure and piece safety while securing the material gain.\nAnswer: P: c7-d6"}
