e has no pawns to block the diagonal (no d-pawn available to push to d4) and blocking with pieces (like Nd4) would only lead to favorable exchanges for Black.\n\nReason: This move maximizes the winning chances by creating an immediate tactical threat against the enemy King while developing the Queen to a safe and active square. It exploits the specific weakness of the f2 square and forces White onto the defensive.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-b6"}
